```

## 5. Controls for the practical

| Key           | Function                      |
| ------------- | ----------------------------- |
| Space / Enter | Boost speed and play audio    |
| Down arrow    | Stop object and audio         |
| H             | High-speed movement and audio |

## 6. Final checklist

- Create `Main` → `MyPath` → both `PathFollow3D` nodes.
- Enter all five Curve3D positions.
- Add SphereMesh and CylinderMesh to the correct children.
- Add `AudioStreamPlayer3D` under both followers and assign the same audio file.
- Attach each script to its corresponding follower.
- Save the scene and run it.

Remember for the exam: `Path3D` defines the route; `PathFollow3D` moves objects along it; `MeshInstance3D` displays the object; `AudioStreamPlayer3D` plays spatial audio.
